  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Cook rice: Rinse the rice until the water runs clear. Put in a small saucepan with 310ml (1¼ cups) water, cover and bring to a simmer over medium heat. Reduce the heat to low and cook for 13 mins or until tender and the water is absorbed. Turn off the heat and stand, covered, for at least 5 mins. Fluff the grains with a fork.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/386091/photos/large/61317_1-fc709eea8d9d204cebcef17e5060914d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, thinly slice the onion. Peel the pumpkin and cut into 3cm chunks. Pick the coriander leaves and finely chop the stems.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/386092/photos/large/61317_2-79a2e37c4609e9ab6245ff0fb9277e0b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soften onion: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the onion, coriander stems and curry paste, stirring regularly, for 3-4 mins until the onion is softened.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/386093/photos/large/61317_3-6031ba8b282514823b1543877b63384f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer curry: Add the pumpkin and 125ml (½ cup) water to the onion mixture and bring to a simmer. Reduce the heat to medium-low and cook, covered, for 12-14 mins until the pumpkin is tender. Stir in the coconut milk and spinach and cook for 1-2 mins until the spinach is wilted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/386094/photos/large/61317_4-8e1d6b6d859d1131951ebf375731a526.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add 1 tsp soy sauce, 1 tsp white vinegar and ½ tsp sugar to the curry and stir to combine. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the rice and curry among bowls. Scatter over the coriander leaves and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/386095/photos/large/61317_5-ffedb2722be841727e3452aedaa91a6e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Like your curries hot? Kick up the heat a notch or two with a scattering of chopped fresh chilli or chilli flakes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/386096/photos/large/61317_6-d9a4b0b50d000bbb11d63f4bace32119.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
